Give the timer thread worker the IHS_ThreadFunction signature.

TimerThreadWorker was declared without a prototype and handed to IHS_ThreadCreate, which
calls it as void (*)(void *). Native builds don't mind, but Emscripten fastcomp keeps one
function table per signature: the worker sits in the "v" table and the thread entry calls
the same index in the "vi" table, which holds some other function. The timer thread then
never runs a task, so discovery broadcasts, pairing and streaming requests are never sent.

